.DS_Store
# Unanchored: the real output dir is app/build, not just ./build.
build/
/captures
.externalNativeBuild
.cxx
local.properties

# The Gradle wrapper is COMMITTED, jar and all (M08).
#
# It was ignored with a README line telling people to run `gradle wrapper`
# once — which means the build needs a Gradle before it can have one, and
# nothing could clone this repository and build it. The jar is 43 KB, the
# version it fetches is pinned in `gradle-wrapper.properties`, and checking it
# in is what upstream Gradle recommends for exactly this reason. The decision
# is recorded in DEVIATIONS.md.

# Signing material never belongs in the repo.
*.jks

# The ONE keystore that is deliberately committed. Signing every CI
# build with a stable key is what lets an update install over the
# previous one — Android refuses a signature change — so an ignored
# keystore here would silently break the in-app updater. Its password is
# public; see android-app/README.md for what that does and does not mean.
!ci-keystore.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties

# The executable specs under tools/ are run with python3/pytest.
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
